{
  "id": "25",
  "title": "Beam RPC",
  "content": "<div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(79, 70, 229, 0.12) 0%, rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.04) 100%); border: 1px solid rgba(79, 70, 229, 0.2); border-left: 4px solid #4F46E5; padding: 32px; margin-bottom: 60px; border-radius: 4px; position: relative; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"position: absolute; top: -20px; right: -20px; opacity: 0.1; transform: rotate(15deg);\"><svg width=\"120\" height=\"120\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4F46E5\" stroke-width=\"1\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"/><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"/></svg></div><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-heading); font-weight: 300;\">**Beam** is a phantom-weight RPC client that bridges the gap between your Photon server and frontend. It provides **absolute type safety** with zero runtime code generation.</p></div><h2>The Intelligence Link</h2><p>Beam isn't a complex library; it's a type-only mirror that reflects your server-side route definitions onto your client-side fetch calls. It eliminates the \"Contract Gap\" without the weight of code generators.</p><div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 24px; margin: 48px 0;\" class=\"bento-grid\"><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(79,70,229,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"> <div style=\"color: #4F46E5; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"m18 16 4-4-4-4\"/><path d=\"m6 8-4 4 4 4\"/><path d=\"m14.5 4-5 16\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">PURE_TYPE_MAP</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">Leverages TypeScript's conditional types to map your entire Photon route tree to a callable proxy object.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(79,70,229,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"><div style=\"color: #4F46E5; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M13 2L3 14h9l-1 8 10-12h-9l1-8z\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">NANOSCALE_SIZE</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">Under 1KB gzipped. It's essentially a thin wrapper around native <code>fetch</code>, optimized for modern bundlers.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(79,70,229,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"><div style=\"color: #4F46E5; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">FAIL_SAFE_AUTO</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">If your server schema changes, your frontend build will fail immediately. Guaranteed structural integrity.</p></div></div><h2>Integration Blueprint</h2><p>Sharing types between server and client without leaking implementation details. Use <code>import type</code> to keep your client bundle clean.</p><pre><code>// 1. Definition (Server Side)\nexport type AppType = typeof app\n\n// 2. Delivery (Client Side)\nimport { createBeam } from '@gravito/beam'\nimport type { AppType } from './server'\n\nconst api = createBeam&lt;AppType&gt;('https://api.v2.node')\n\n// 3. Execution (Full IntelliSense)\nconst res = await api.users[':id'].profile.$get({\n  param: { id: 'usr_99' }\n})</code></pre><div style=\"background: rgba(79, 70, 229, 0.05); border: 1px solid rgba(79, 70, 229, 0.1); border-left: 4px solid #4F46E5; padding: 24px; margin: 40px 0; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;\"><h4 style=\"margin: 0 0 10px 0; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 900; color: #4F46E5; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em;\">// BEAM_SPEC: ZERO_PROXIED_OVERHEAD</h4><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 15px; font-style: italic; color: var(--text-heading); opacity: 0.9; border: none; padding: 0;\">Beam uses ES6 Proxies to intercept calls. This means the object tree doesn't exist in memory until you touch it—infinite routes, O(1) memory footprint.</p></div><h2>Performance: Bundle Density</h2><p>Comparing RPC client weights for modern frontend applications.</p><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; margin: 40px 0; border-radius: 4px;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 30px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; color: #4F46E5; margin-bottom: 12px; font-family: var(--font-technical);\"><span>BEAM_RPC_CLIENT</span> <span>&lt; 0.8KB</span></div><div style=\"height: 8px; background: rgba(79,70,229,0.1); width: 100%; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"height: 100%; width: 5%; background: #4F46E5; box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(79,70,229,0.5);\"></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; color: #6B7280; margin-bottom: 12px; font-family: var(--font-technical);\"><span>TRPC_CLIENT_STACK</span> <span>~45.0KB</span></div><div style=\"height: 8px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); width: 100%; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"height: 100%; width: 90%; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.2);\"></div></div></div><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; font-family: var(--font-technical); border: none; padding: 0;\">// METRIC: BEAM IS VIRTUALLY INVISIBLE IN THE FINAL BUNDLE</p></div><div style=\"background: linear-gradient(to right, rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.1), transparent); border-left: 4px solid #06B6D4; padding: 24px; margin-top: 60px; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;\"><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500; font-style: italic; border: none; padding: 0; color: var(--text-heading);\">**Architect's Insight:** Complex code generation is the enemy of agility. Beam treats your server's Photon instance as the ultimate source of truth, ensuring that your types are always in sync without a single line of generated glue code.</p></div>",
